<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Auschwitz concentration camp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Auschwitz-Birkenau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Auschwitz</a> was the largest Nazi German concentration and extermination camp, built from 1940 near the Polish town of Oświęcim, which the Germans called Auschwitz. About 1.1 million people were murdered there, around a million of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, most in the gas chambers of Auschwitz II–Birkenau. More than 400,000 Hungarian Jews were deported there in 1944. Soviet troops liberated it on 27 January 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/auschwitz-concentration-camp.jpg" alt="Auschwitz concentration camp" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva; derivative work by Georgfotoart · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Auschwitz_I_(22_May_2010)_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
